    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Fudge is Michael Kiwanuka’s fifth studio album, released by Polydor in 2026. It presents a looser, more instinctive side of his songwriting, blending warm soul, blues-rooted rock, funk-inflected grooves, and psychedelic color. Across twelve tracks—including “Summer Clothes,” “California,” “Stars,” and “Sing”—Kiwanuka favors expressive vocals, spacious arrangements, and an atmosphere of creative freedom over the grand, tightly constructed drama of some of his earlier work.\n\nInspired in part by Chick Corea’s encouragement to follow instinct rather than outside expectations, the album is vibrant, intimate, and deeply human. Its relaxed musical feel gives the songs room to move between tenderness, melancholy, and playful energy, while Kiwanuka’s understated delivery remains the emotional center. Fudge was also received as a particularly poignant release because it was recorded alongside Small Changes and arrived amid serious health news, lending its celebration of spontaneity an added bittersweet resonance.",
